Here is the Rust code that applies ROT13 to upper/lowercase letters and preserves other characters.

```rust
use serde_json::Value;

pub fn solve(input: Value) -> Value {
    match input {
        Value::String(s) => {
            let mut result = String::new();
            for c in s.chars() {
                if c.is_ascii_uppercase() {
                    result.push((c as u8 + 13) as char);
                } else if c.is_ascii_lowercase() {
                    result.push((c as u8 - 13) as char);
                } else {
                    result.push(c);
                }
            }
            Value::String(result)
        },
        _ => input,
    }
}
```

This function will convert all uppercase letters to lowercase letters and vice versa. It will leave other characters as they are. The function will return the input value unchanged if it is not a string.
